    "set_python_instance_state is called by construct_python_object (constructor.py:598) and construct_python_object_apply (:627); construct_python_object_new calls construct_python_object_apply (:636). The walker stops because construct_python_object and construct_python_object_new are only referenced as arguments to add_multi_constructor (review reasons: lib3/yaml/constructor.py:696 and :700). Those registrations put them in FullConstructor.yaml_multi_constructors under the python/object: and python/object/new: tag prefixes, and BaseConstructor.construct_object (:74-95) looks the node's tag prefix up in that table and calls the constructor, so a document with !!python/object/new: (or !!python/object:) and a state reaches set_python_instance_state. construct_object is reached from get_single_data / get_data -> construct_document, which yaml.load and yaml.load_all call on the loader they build; both default to FullLoader in 5.3 (__init__.py:110, :125), and full_load / full_load_all pass FullLoader explicitly (:142, :152). FullLoader (loader.py:21) and CFullLoader (cyaml.py:30, exported as yaml.CFullLoader only when libyaml is installed) inherit FullConstructor and so its table. Checked against the record's tree 2f463cf (tag 5.3), lib3/ copy (lib/ is the Python 2 copy of the same code) on 2026-11-04."
